    "notes": "ONE part with 2 staves (grand staff); the right hand's two voices (bars 1-2, 9, 13-15) belong to that part and must not become separate parts. 16 bars: quarter pickup in 4/4 (numeric) and incomplete 3-beat final bar; meters 3/4 (bar 3), 5/8 beamed 3+2 (4-5), 7/8 beamed 2+2+3 (6-7), 2/4 (8), 3/2 (9), 9/8 (10-11), 2/2 with cut symbol (12-13), 4/4 with C symbol (14-15); bars 3, 6, 9 and 12 start systems with a new meter, so courtesy signatures end the previous systems. Whole-bar rests in one staff only: LH bar 3 (3/4), RH bar 12 (2/2). Ties: RH a''2~a''8 over the system break and the 4/4->3/4 change (2->3), c'''4~c'''16 (bar 2), e''4.~e''8 (5), f''2~f''8 (13), LH chord <c e>4.~ over the barline 10->11. LH <e, b,>2.. fills a 7/8 bar. Fermatas on the final chords of both staves.",
